767 1074 "First, notice that the $2$nd row of our determinant is almost equal to the $3$rd row. So, we can rewrite the given determinant, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 144 & 158 & 103 \\\\ 144 & 158 & 102\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 144+0 & 158+0 & 102+1 \\\\ 144 & 158 & 102\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, using the linearity property of determinants, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 144+0 & 158+0 & 102+1 \\\\ 144 & 158 & 102\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 144 & 158 & 102 \\\\ 144 & 158 & 102\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 144 & 158 & 102\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first determinant must be zero since it has two identical rows, while the second determinant can be expanded across the $2$nd row, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 144 & 158 & 102 \\\\ 144 & 158 & 102\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 144 & 158 & 102\\end{aligned}| & =0+1(-1)^{2+3}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 144 & 158\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(2\\cdot 158-4\\cdot 144) \\\\  & =-(316-576) \\\\  & =260\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534779 17592186045417 true] [17592186435768 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435766 13194139534779 17592186045417 true] [17592186435768 1069 "q-130780" 13194139534779 17592186045417 true] [17592186435768 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534779 17592186045417 true] [17592186435768 1071 "Given that \n$|\\begin{aligned}a & b & c \\\\ -3 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|=3,$\nfind \n$|\\begin{aligned}a-2 & b & c \\\\ -3 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|.$" 13194139534779 17592186045417 true] [17592186435768 1072 #uuid "788f9347-638e-5e07-bc97-727179291d72" 13194139534779 17592186045417 true] [17592186435768 1074 "We \"factor out\" the given determinant from the determinant we would like to find:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}a-2 & b & c \\\\ -3 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}a-2 & b+0 & c+0 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the linearity property of determinants and expanding the second determinant across the $1$st row, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}a-2 & b+0 & c+0 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & ={{|\\begin{aligned}a & b & c \\\\ -3 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|}_{⏟}}_{3}+|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3-2(-1)^{1+1}|\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3-2\\cdot (5+1) \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534779 17592186045417 true] [17592186435769 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435764 13194139534779 17592186045417 true] [17592186435769 1069 "q-130532" 13194139534779 17592186045417 true] [17592186435769 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534779 17592186045417 true] [17592186435769 1071 "Find $|{A}^{-1}|,$ if $A=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 6\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534779 17592186045417 true] [17592186435769 1072 #uuid "8501cdd8-7879-5e81-a6ba-962c1d7f9129" 13194139534779 17592186045417 true] [17592186435769 1074 "Given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\n|{A}^{-1}|=\\frac{1}{|A|}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $|A|$ using a Laplace expansion across the $2$nd row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A| & =|\\begin{aligned}-5 & -3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 6\\end{aligned}|+1(-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}|+2(-1)^{2+3}|\\begin{aligned}-5 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(-18+16)+(-30-4)-2(20+3) \\\\  & =-4-34-46 \\\\  & =-84\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n|{A}^{-1}|=\\frac{1}{|A|}=-\\frac{1}{84}.\n$$" 13194139534779 17592186045417 true] [17592186435770 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435765 13194139534779 17592186045417 true] [17592186435770 1069 "q-42583" 13194139534779 17592186045417 true] [17592186435770 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534779 17592186045417 true] [17592186435770 1071 "Find $|{A}^{-1}|,$ if $A=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 6 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534779 17592186045417 true] [17592186435770 1072 #uuid "eee0d247-b841-57bb-b4de-7b3606da042f" 13194139534779 17592186045417 true] [17592186435770 1074 "Given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\n|{A}^{-1}|=\\frac{1}{|A|}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $|A|$ using a Laplace expansion across the $2$nd row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A| & =|\\begin{aligned}7 & 6 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}6 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}|+2(-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}|-1(-1)^{2+3}|\\begin{aligned}7 & 6 \\\\ 5 & -5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(12-15)+2(14+15)+(-35-30) \\\\  & =3+58-65 \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n|{A}^{-1}|=\\frac{1}{|A|}=-\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$" 13194139534779 17592186045417 true] [17592186435771 1058 #edb/ref 17592186435772 13194139534779 17592186045417 true] [17592186435771 1062 #uuid "1d161349-e4e8-5aa1-b4e7-f6d11a6bf9dc" 13194139534779 17592186045417 true] [17592186435771 1063 #edb/ref 17592186435767 13194139534779 17592186045417 true] [17592186435772 1062 #uuid "77ada6f1-1dfa-54e5-88ae-7663f6d4729f" 13194139534779 17592186045417 true] [17592186435772 1063 #edb/ref 17592186435768 13194139534779 17592186045417 true] [17592186435773 1058 #edb/ref 17592186435775 13194139534779 17592186045417 true] [17592186435773 1062 #uuid "8a2caee0-7a00-5713-8017-f3895a8befc5" 13194139534779 17592186045417 true] [17592186435773 1063 #edb/ref 17592186354637 13194139534779 17592186045417 true] [17592186435774 1058 #edb/ref 17592186435773 13194139534779 17592186045417 true] [17592186435774 1062 #uuid "9f1a9a64-1470-537f-a2d2-3bc970633d21" 13194139534779 17592186045417 true] [17592186435774 1063 #edb/ref 17592186435770 13194139534779